  m_Name: african-derived
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WordInfo
  words:
  - african-derived
  info: "African-derived bees, also known as Africanized bees or \u201Ckiller bees,\u201D
    are hybrid honey bees produced by crossbreeding African and European subspecies
    of the Western honey bee. They were introduced to Brazil in 1956 to increase
    honey production but escaped captivity and spread throughout South and Central
    America, eventually reaching parts of the southern United States. Africanized
    bees are significantly more defensive than other honey bees, responding more
    quickly, attacking in greater numbers, and pursuing perceived threats over longer
    distances.\n\nSource - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Africanized_bee "
  image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 7fda69f2bb1adb54bbd5541e5cb7b378, type: 3}
